# Camera movement
@scenario tutorial_lesson_13
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide point]
pip: This example pans and zooms the background while Pip stays in place.
[if !tutorial_still]
timeline {
  parallel {
    move "bg_current" { x:-64 y:-36 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
    scale "bg_current" { sx:1.08 sy:1.08 dur:640 easing:ease_out }
  }
}
[endif]
pip: Compare the two keyframes in Puppeteer. Watch the far edge as the scale increases.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: Why pair a small pan with a zoom?
> To keep the frame filled while the subject shifts. -> correct
> To change the speaker name. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: A zoom can cover the edge exposed by a pan. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: A zoom can cover the edge exposed by a pan.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_13]
[flag tutorial_done_13]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
